node_modules/
dist/
public/wasm/
public/models/selfie_multiclass_256x256.tflite
.DS_Store
*.local

# Secrets. This repo is public — Supabase keys and any other env values live in
# .env files locally and in the Vercel dashboard, never in git.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Calibration photographs — the README, never the faces. See calib/README.md.
# Both spellings: the tools default to .calib/, older docs used calib/.
calib/*
!calib/README.md
.calib/
.reel-cache/
.vercel

# Working footage, and anything the app exported that got dropped in here.
#
# This repo is public, and the files in question are VIDEO OF PEOPLE'S FACES —
# source clips for edits, rendered rundowns, scan stills. None of it belongs in
# a public history, and none of it is recoverable once pushed: a later delete
# removes it from the working tree and leaves it in every clone.
#
# It nearly happened. Sorting exports into ~/TrueMax on a case-insensitive
# filesystem created those folders INSIDE this repo, because macOS treats
# ~/TrueMax and ~/truemax as one directory, and they landed untracked next to
# package.json. Loose fatthor-*.mp4 clips and a clips/ folder were already
# sitting there for the same reason: the repo root is where you happen to be
# standing when a file arrives.
#
# Videos are ignored wholesale — no video file is tracked in this repo and none
# should be. Images are NOT, because the brand marks and demo portraits under
# public/ are legitimately versioned; face images are covered by calib/ above.
*.mp4
*.mov
*.m4v
*.webm
clips/

# The export folders, in every casing the sorter might produce.
[Rr]eels/
[Rr]undowns/
[Ss]cans/
[Uu]nsorted/
Verdict?cards/

# Vite's dependency-optimiser cache. Written into the repo root whenever the
# dev server runs, including from the headless frame-check harness, so it turns
# up as an untracked directory after any session that looked at a rendered
# frame. A build cache, not source.
.vite/
supabase/.temp/

# Local visual exports created by the renderer and frame-check tools.
exports/

# Contact sheets from tools/rundown-sheet.mjs — regenerate, never commit.
.rundown-sheet/
